# ╔═╡ 673ab792-25a1-4ff9-b886-f356b612306a
md"
---
###### 3.8.2 Digital Integration
(cf. Walck, 2023, p.82f)

$myIntegral: Function \times R \times R \times R \rightarrow R$

$myIntegral: f \rightarrow F$

$myIntegral: (f, dt, a, b) \mapsto \int_a^b f\;dt$

"

# ╔═╡ 635f5336-6d07-4b81-9c43-dcd9402687cd
md"
We define *two* methods for function $myIntegral$. This implements the *Midpoint Rule* (Walck, 2024, p.84; Richter et al., 2024, p.453). The *first* method takes as first *argument* a *continuous* function $f$ in *closed* form wheras the *second* method takes as first argument a *discretisized* version of $f$. This is a *vector* of function *values*. 

The first method is necessary to compute $F$ from continuous $f$ in closed form. The second methods is necessary to obtain $F$ from a discretisized form of $f$ when we obtained $f$ from $f'$ with the first method from a continuous closed $f'$. 

"

# ╔═╡ afcc8e4b-d561-4c67-b349-cdaa11144855
md"
---
###### 1. Method: Definite Integral F(x) = $\int_a^b f(x)dx$ from Closed Form *Continuous Function* $f(x)$

$\left.F(x)\right|_a^b = \int_a^b f(x)dx \approx c + \Delta x \sum_{i=1}^b f(x_i)$

$a \le x_i \le b, x_i + \Delta x = x_{i+1}.$

"

# ╔═╡ 8a00be3c-1762-46f5-8509-206006237d01
# definite integral of function f
myIntegral(f::Function, Δx::Float64, a::Float64, b::Float64; c=0.0)::Float64 =      
	c + Δx * sum([f(x) for x in a + Δx/2.0:Δx:b - Δx/2.0])

# ╔═╡ 985ef39e-4be8-4626-9603-fe4ae2f54545
md"
###### 2. Method: Approximation of Definite Integral from *Vector* of Discretized *Function* Values 

$\left.F(x)\right |_a^b \approx c + \Delta x\sum_{i=1}^n f_x[i]$


where: 

$f_x[i] = f(x_i); a \le x_i \le b, x_i + \Delta x = x_{i+1},$

$[...,f_x[i],...] \;;\; i=1,...,n$ is the *vector* of function values and 

$length([...,f_x[i],...] = n$ 

is its *length* $n$ (= *number* $n$ of vector *components*).

There is a *constraint* between upper integration limit $x = b - a$, $length([...,f_x[i],...]\ and\ \Delta x$:

$x = length([...,f_x[i],...]) \cdot \Delta x = n \Delta x$

and mappings

$(x, \frac{1}{\Delta x}) \mapsto n \left(= length([...,f_xx[i],...])\right)$

$(x, n) \mapsto \frac{x}{n} = \Delta x.$

"

# ╔═╡ 1d33ad08-fa2d-4c7c-9329-330159d5d56c
# integration of vector of values
myIntegral(fs::Vector{Float64}, Δx::Float64; c=0.0)::Tuple{Float64, Float64} =    
	# value by generator, integration limit x
	c + Δx * sum((f for f in fs)), length(fs) * Δx # length(fs) * Δx = n

